<Legal title="Disclaimer" seoTitle="Disclaimer | promptbeen ChatGPT Photo Prompts" description="Disclaimer for promptbeen: our ChatGPT AI photo editing prompts are starting points with no guaranteed results, and we are not affiliated with OpenAI.">
  <h2>No affiliation with OpenAI</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} is an independent website. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by OpenAI. ChatGPT is a trademark of OpenAI, and we use the name only to describe what our prompts are meant for. When we say a prompt works with ChatGPT, that is our own experience and not a statement from OpenAI.</p>
  <h2>Sample images</h2>
  <p>Preview images on this site are illustrations of each style and are not outputs from any specific AI model. Do not expect your own result to look identical to a preview.</p>
  <h2>Results are not guaranteed</h2>
  <p>Every prompt on promptbeen is a starting point. Output depends on your photo, your account plan, your region and the model version in use. Features and limits inside ChatGPT may change without notice. We cannot promise that any prompt will give you a particular look.</p>
  <h3>Why results vary</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your photo:</strong> a sharp, well-lit portrait behaves differently from a dark, blurry or crowded photo, even with the same prompt.</li>
    <li><strong>The ChatGPT version:</strong> a newer or older model may read the same words differently, and a feature you saw in a video may not be in your plan.</li>
    <li><strong>Your region:</strong> some features arrive later, or not at all, in certain countries.</li>
    <li><strong>Your wording:</strong> changing one detail, such as the lighting or the pose, can change the whole picture.</li>
    <li><strong>Chance:</strong> AI tools can give a different answer each time you run the same prompt.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If a result is off, try again, add one detail at a time, or describe what to keep as well as what to change. The <a href="/ai-photo-prompt-tool/">prompt tool</a> and our <a href="/blog/">blog guides</a> can help.</p>
  <h2>Responsible use of AI images</h2>
  <p>Editing a photo with AI is easy, which makes it easy to do harm by accident. Please keep to these basics.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Rights:</strong> only edit photos you own or have permission to edit.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent:</strong> ask the people in a photo before you edit and share it, especially for couple or family photos.</li>
    <li><strong>No deception:</strong> do not create misleading or harmful images of real people, fake documents, or edits meant to pass as real evidence.</li>
    <li><strong>No sexualising minors,</strong> and no non-consensual intimate imagery, ever.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You are responsible for what you create and share. We do not see your photos, so we cannot check them for you.</p>
  <h2>No professional advice</h2>
  <p>Content on this site is for general information only. It is not medical, legal, financial or other professional advice. If you need advice, ask a qualified person.</p>
  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>Our pages may link to other websites, including OpenAI. We do not control those sites and do not endorse them. Their content, availability and privacy practices are their own, and may change after we link to them.</p>
  <h2>Prompts are patterns, not endorsements</h2>
  <p>Many prompts here are written in the style of patterns people share online, such as those behind ChatGPT photo editing prompts trending on Instagram. We write or adapt them as general patterns. A prompt that follows a popular look does not mean we are connected to the person who made it popular, and it does not mean any creator, brand or company endorses {SITE.name}.</p>
  <h2>No professional or commercial advice</h2>
  <p>Some guides discuss photos for business profiles, shop listings or social media. Those tips are about picture style only. They are not advice on advertising rules, marketing results or legal rights in images. If a photo matters for a contract, a listing or an official purpose, ask a qualified person, and do not rely on an AI edit to represent something that is not true.</p>
  <h2>Web stories and blog guides</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/web-stories/">web stories</a> and <a href="/blog/">blog guides</a> are written to help you understand ChatGPT AI photo editing prompts. They reflect what we knew when we wrote them. Where a guide mentions a feature, a menu name or a limit inside ChatGPT, check it against the app you are using, because OpenAI may change these things without telling us.</p>
  <h2>Community-style content</h2>
  <p>The site has no public comments or user posts. Prompt suggestions sent to us are reviewed and may be edited before they are published. We cannot check every claim a sender makes, so please treat any prompt as a starting point and test it on a photo you are happy to experiment with.</p>
  <h2>Your device and browser</h2>
  <p>Copy Prompt buttons copy text to your clipboard on your own device. Whether that works depends on your browser and its permissions. If a button does not copy, select the text by hand and copy it that way. We are not responsible for lost or overwritten clipboard contents, so check what you paste before you send it to ChatGPT.</p>
  <h2>Sensitive photos</h2>
  <p>Think carefully before you edit photos of children, private moments or anything you would not want shared. Once a photo has been uploaded to any AI service, what happens to it is governed by that service, not by promptbeen.</p>
